WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:19.258
"Wow," Cole said as Nora started crying even harder.

2
00:00:19.259 --> 00:00:21.703
"It looks like we just solved the mystery."

3
00:00:21.704 --> 00:00:24.159
"Yeah," Henry agreed.

4
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.990
"So my funny feeling was wrong," he thought.

5
00:00:27.991 --> 00:00:32.039
He'd been convinced that Nora was too little to be the thief.

6
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.833
But now, here she was, confessing to the crime.

7
00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:40.677
"I'm sorry, Maggie!" Nora blurted out between sobs.

8
00:00:40.678 --> 00:00:43.830
"I didn't think you'd mind if I took it."

9
00:00:43.831 --> 00:00:48.636
"You didn't think I'd mind?" Maggie echoed in disbelief.

10
00:00:48.637 --> 00:00:55.189
"Are you crazy? Why wouldn't I mind? You took my money!"

11
00:00:55.190 --> 00:01:00.249
"Huh?" Nora blinked and sniffled. "What money?"

12
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.020
"The money you grabbed from the cashbox," Cole said.

13
00:01:04.021 --> 00:01:06.755
"Those two older girls saw you take it."

14
00:01:06.756 --> 00:01:12.362
Henry was starting to get that funny feeling again. "Wait," he said.

15
00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:14.743
"The girls didn't say that.

16
00:01:14.744 --> 00:01:20.338
They just said they saw Nora grabbing something from the table and looking sneaky.

17
00:01:20.339 --> 00:01:22.740
What did you take, Nora?"

18
00:01:22.741 --> 00:01:27.979
"None of your business," Nora said. She wasn't crying anymore.

19
00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.062
Now she was starting to look stubborn.

20
00:01:31.063 --> 00:01:36.085
Henry stared at her. Something about this didn't make sense.

21
00:01:36.086 --> 00:01:39.349
He just wished he could figure out what it was.

22
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:43.978
"You'd better tell me right now, Nora!" Maggie exclaimed.

23
00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:47.831
"You can't make me," Nora yelled back.

24
00:01:47.832 --> 00:01:55.130
"Yeah!" Nora's friend added. "You can't order her around. She's a princess!"

25
00:01:55.131 --> 00:01:58.552
Just then Nathan hurried out of the house.

26
00:01:58.553 --> 00:02:02.557
"What's going on out here?" he asked.

27
00:02:02.558 --> 00:02:08.289
"Hi, Nathan," Henry said. "We were just talking to your sister."

28
00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:13.191
"No, they weren't!" Nora started to cry again.

29
00:02:13.192 --> 00:02:18.062
"They were trying to drag me off to jail!"

30
00:02:18.063 --> 00:02:22.081
"What?" Now Nathan looked really confused.

31
00:02:22.082 --> 00:02:25.965
"She's exaggerating," Maggie said.

32
00:02:25.966 --> 00:02:31.045
"We were just trying to get my money back. Nora stole it!"

33
00:02:31.046 --> 00:02:35.775
Nathan shook his head. "Nora didn't take that money."

34
00:02:35.776 --> 00:02:41.262
"Yeah!" Nora stuck out her tongue at Maggie. "I didn't take your money."

35
00:02:41.263 --> 00:02:47.563
"Yes, you did!" Maggie said. "You just confessed, remember?"

36
00:02:47.564 --> 00:02:53.290
"No way." Nora looked stubborn again. "I didn't take any money.

37
00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:56.718
All I took was an extra cup of lemonade!"

38
00:02:56.719 --> 00:03:02.165
Everyone looked surprised. "Extra lemonade?" Cole said.

39
00:03:02.166 --> 00:03:08.937
"Oh . . ." Henry nodded. "That must be what those teenage girls saw her doing.

40
00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:11.800
Nora wasn't sneaking around to steal the money.

41
00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:15.656
She was just sneaking some extra lemonade."

42
00:03:15.657 --> 00:03:19.118
"How do we know she didn't do both things?

43
00:03:19.119 --> 00:03:23.504
She just admitted that she's a lemonade thief," Maggie said.

44
00:03:23.505 --> 00:03:26.241
"She might be a money thief too!"

45
00:03:26.242 --> 00:03:29.791
"Come on, Maggie," Nathan said.

46
00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:33.727
"Nora might be sneaky enough to grab some extra lemonade.

47
00:03:33.728 --> 00:03:37.042
But she wouldn't steal your cash."

48
00:03:37.043 --> 00:03:43.758
"Maybe not on her own," Maggie said, glancing from Nora to Nathan and then back again.

49
00:03:43.759 --> 00:03:50.068
Nathan folded his arms across his chest. "What do you mean?" he asked.

50
00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:56.618
"Cole was right. It was probably all your idea!" Maggie burst out.

51
00:03:56.619 --> 00:04:00.542
"Wait, I didn't say that!" Cole chimed in.

52
00:04:00.543 --> 00:04:05.872
Maggie didn't pay any attention to him. She was still staring at Nathan.

53
00:04:05.873 --> 00:04:13.617
"You two were wandering past and saw that I was making tons of money at my lemonade stand," she said.

54
00:04:13.618 --> 00:04:15.964
"So you got greedy."

55
00:04:15.965 --> 00:04:19.183
She narrowed her eyes and looked around.

56
00:04:19.184 --> 00:04:23.733
Henry could tell she was pausing to make her story sound more dramatic.

57
00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:26.678
It was definitely a dramatic story.

58
00:04:26.679 --> 00:04:30.112
But Henry still wasn't convinced that it was true.

59
00:04:30.113 --> 00:04:36.378
That funny feeling inside him was stronger than ever, and he needed time to think about it.

60
00:04:36.379 --> 00:04:39.347
"Maggie . . . ," he started to say.

61
00:04:39.348 --> 00:04:45.544
"That's when you made your plan," Maggie went on, glaring at Nathan and ignoring Henry.

62
00:04:45.545 --> 00:04:50.117
"You walked over and bought some lemonade for yourself and Nora.

63
00:04:50.118 --> 00:04:54.049
You even borrowed money from Mrs. Martin to pay for it!"

64
00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:59.205
"They did?" Henry was surprised. He hadn't known that.

65
00:04:59.206 --> 00:05:01.964
Maggie was still staring at Nathan.

66
00:05:01.965 --> 00:05:07.163
"Then you started talking to me, distracting me on purpose.

67
00:05:07.164 --> 00:05:13.883
That gave your sneaky little sister time to grab the money out of the cashbox while my back was turned.

68
00:05:13.884 --> 00:05:20.410
Then all she had to do was hide it and pretend she didn't know anything. I think she—"

69
00:05:20.411 --> 00:05:27.349
"Hold on, Maggie," Henry interrupted. "I just realized something.

70
00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.053
Nora couldn't have taken your money."

71
00:05:30.054 --> 00:05:35.275
Maggie, Cole, Nathan, and even Nora all turned to stare at him.

72
00:05:35.276 --> 00:05:38.853
"What are you talking about, Henry?" Maggie said.

73
00:05:38.854 --> 00:05:43.300
"Of course she did! Who else could have done it?"

74
00:05:43.301 --> 00:05:50.598
"I don't know." Henry shrugged. "But it wasn't Nora. You said it yourself.

75
00:05:50.599 --> 00:05:54.741
All she had to do was hide that money after she took it."

76
00:05:54.742 --> 00:05:58.326
"Right," Maggie said. "So?"

77
00:05:58.327 --> 00:06:01.688
"So don't you see?" Henry continued.

78
00:06:01.689 --> 00:06:07.291
"She couldn't hide it because she had nowhere to put it. Remember?

79
00:06:07.292 --> 00:06:12.994
Nora and Nathan stopped by the lemonade stand on their way home from the swimming pool.

80
00:06:12.995 --> 00:06:20.536
All they had on were their bathing suits!"
